localpasskey (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Feature: deleting moves passkeys to a trash; restore them or permanently
    delete one at a time by typing its site name (CLI `restore`/`purge`, window
    Trash view).
  * Feature: CTAP 2.1 credential management, so Chrome's Settings > Security
    keys > Sign-in data lists and deletes passkeys once a PIN is set; deleting
    there moves the passkey to the trash.
  * Feature: an optional PIN (`localpasskey pin`, window Security Key PIN
    dialog), needed by browsers to list or delete passkeys; passkey management
    still asks for your password.
  * Feature: the window can do everything the CLI does: bulk move to trash by
    site or all, restore, permanently delete, PIN.
  * Change: credentials.json is now format 2 (still reads format 1);
    downgrading to 0.1.1 refuses the file instead of bringing trashed passkeys
    back.
  * Docs: README limitations corrected (which missing extensions matter and
    which do not).

 -- LocalPasskey Maintainers <maintainers@localpasskey.invalid>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

localpasskey (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: a "pick this authenticator" touch followed by a registration left
    the approval armed, so a later sign-in to any site could be signed
    without a confirmation dialog.
  * Fix: a touch approval also survived a sign-in that found no passkey and
    covered the following request.
  * Fix: a transient accept() error (for example, a full file-descriptor
    table) permanently stopped the control socket.
  * Perf: sign-ins no longer rewrite the whole credential file with two
    fsyncs just to bump "last used"; the timestamp is kept at the minute
    resolution the CLI and window display.
  * Perf: silent (user-presence-free) assertions no longer write the store,
    and the CBOR decoder no longer allocates per item.
  * 17 simplifications; unused code removed.

 -- LocalPasskey Maintainers <maintainers@localpasskey.invalid>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 07:30:00 +0000

